IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `bnra-types`
IMPORT `bnra-part2-names`

-- Tests for Part 2, ss 15 to 24.  Thresholds read off the text: 60 days' reservation (s 16(4));
-- waiting periods of one, two and six years, and 3 months (s 17(2), (3)); 6 weeks to change a
-- name (s 17(4)); 12 months for a resemblance application (s 17(7)); 14 days for the notices
-- in ss 19, 20, 22; at least 30 days for objection (s 23); 12 months to restore (s 24).
-- #TRACE results are printed, not asserted; NOTES.md records them.

§ `Tests -- Part 2, ss 15 to 24`

§§ `15. Use of business names`

-- Use of Name Facts: required to be registered, registered, uses another name, not required in
-- respect of that name under s 4, use otherwise prohibited.
`registered but using another name` MEANS `Use of Name Facts` OF TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE
`registered, using another name that s 4 exempts` MEANS `Use of Name Facts` OF TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  FALSE
`registered and using only the registered name` MEANS `Use of Name Facts` OF TRUE,  TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`not registered but using another name` MEANS `Use of Name Facts` OF TRUE,  FALSE, TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE
`not required to register and using another name` MEANS `Use of Name Facts` OF FALSE, TRUE,  TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE
`registered name whose use is prohibited by another law` MEANS `Use of Name Facts` OF TRUE,  TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, TRUE

#ASSERT `the person contravenes section 15(1)` `registered but using another name`
#ASSERT NOT `the person contravenes section 15(1)` `registered, using another name that s 4 exempts`
#ASSERT NOT `the person contravenes section 15(1)` `registered and using only the registered name`
#ASSERT NOT `the person contravenes section 15(1)` `not registered but using another name`
#ASSERT NOT `the person contravenes section 15(1)` `not required to register and using another name`
#ASSERT `registration authorises the use of the registered business name` `registered and using only the registered name`
#ASSERT NOT `registration authorises the use of the registered business name` `registered name whose use is prohibited by another law`

§§ `16. Reservation of business names`

`no public interest concern` MEANS `Public Interest Facts` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`an unlawful purpose concern` MEANS `Public Interest Facts` OF TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE
`a national interest concern` MEANS `Public Interest Facts` OF FALSE, TRUE,  FALSE
`a certificate only` MEANS `Public Interest Facts` OF FALSE, FALSE, TRUE

`an approval notified on 1 March 2026` MEANS `approved` (YMD 2026 3 1) 0
`an approval notified on 1 March 2026 and extended once` MEANS `approved` (YMD 2026 3 1) 1
`a refusal notified on 5 March 2026` MEANS `refused` (YMD 2026 3 5)

-- Reservation Facts: lodged, good faith, name registrable, public interest facts, foreign company
-- not registered, date received, decision.
`a good application` MEANS `Reservation Facts` OF TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  `no public interest concern`, FALSE, YMD 2026 3 1, `an approval notified on 1 March 2026`
`an application not made in good faith` MEANS `Reservation Facts` OF TRUE,  FALSE, TRUE,  `no public interest concern`, FALSE, YMD 2026 3 1, `an approval notified on 1 March 2026`
`an application for a name that could not be registered` MEANS `Reservation Facts` OF TRUE,  TRUE,  FALSE, `no public interest concern`, FALSE, YMD 2026 3 1, `an approval notified on 1 March 2026`
`an application for an unlawful business` MEANS `Reservation Facts` OF TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  `an unlawful purpose concern`, FALSE, YMD 2026 3 1, `an approval notified on 1 March 2026`
`an application contrary to the national interest` MEANS `Reservation Facts` OF TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  `a national interest concern`, FALSE, YMD 2026 3 1, `an approval notified on 1 March 2026`
`an application resting only on the Minister's certificate` MEANS `Reservation Facts` OF TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  `a certificate only`, FALSE, YMD 2026 3 1, `an approval notified on 1 March 2026`
`an application by an unregistered foreign company` MEANS `Reservation Facts` OF TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  `no public interest concern`, TRUE,  YMD 2026 3 1, `an approval notified on 1 March 2026`
`an application not lodged` MEANS `Reservation Facts` OF FALSE, TRUE,  TRUE,  `no public interest concern`, FALSE, YMD 2026 3 1, `an approval notified on 1 March 2026`
`an approved application extended once` MEANS `Reservation Facts` OF TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  `no public interest concern`, FALSE, YMD 2026 3 1, `an approval notified on 1 March 2026 and extended once`
`a refused application` MEANS `Reservation Facts` OF TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  `no public interest concern`, FALSE, YMD 2026 3 1, `a refusal notified on 5 March 2026`

#ASSERT `the Registrar may approve the reservation` `a good application`
#ASSERT NOT `the Registrar may approve the reservation` `an application not made in good faith`
#ASSERT NOT `the Registrar may approve the reservation` `an application for a name that could not be registered`
#ASSERT NOT `the Registrar may approve the reservation` `an application for an unlawful business`
#ASSERT NOT `the Registrar may approve the reservation` `an application contrary to the national interest`
#ASSERT NOT `the Registrar may approve the reservation` `an application by an unregistered foreign company`
#ASSERT NOT `the Registrar may approve the reservation` `an application not lodged`
#ASSERT `the Registrar must refuse to approve the reservation` `an application for an unlawful business`
#ASSERT `the Registrar must refuse to approve the reservation` `an application contrary to the national interest`
#ASSERT `the Registrar must refuse to approve the reservation` `an application by an unregistered foreign company`
-- s 13(1) makes the certificate conclusive only for ss 9(b) and 12(1)(a)(ii), so it does not by itself require refusal here
#ASSERT NOT `the Registrar must refuse to approve the reservation` `an application resting only on the Minister's certificate`
#ASSERT NOT `the Registrar must refuse to approve the reservation` `a good application`

-- 16(4): 60 days after notice of approval (1 March + 60 = 30 April), a further 60 (29 June)
#ASSERT `the last day of the reservation` `a good application` EQUALS YMD 2026 4 30
#ASSERT `the last day of the reservation` `an approved application extended once` EQUALS YMD 2026 6 29
#ASSERT `the last day of the reservation` `a refused application` EQUALS YMD 2026 3 5
#ASSERT NOT `the name is reserved on the date` `a good application` (YMD 2026 2 28)
#ASSERT `the name is reserved on the date` `a good application` (YMD 2026 3 1)
#ASSERT `the name is reserved on the date` `a good application` (YMD 2026 4 30)
#ASSERT NOT `the name is reserved on the date` `a good application` (YMD 2026 5 1)
#ASSERT `the name is reserved on the date` `an approved application extended once` (YMD 2026 5 1)
#ASSERT `the name is reserved on the date` `a refused application` (YMD 2026 3 5)
#ASSERT NOT `the name is reserved on the date` `a refused application` (YMD 2026 3 6)

§§ `17. Restrictions on registration of business names`

-- Name Restriction Facts: undesirable, identical to another registered name or a corporation or
-- limited partnership, identical to a reserved name, of a kind the Minister directed not to
-- accept, Minister consents.  Then whether s 17(3) permits registration.
`an acceptable name` MEANS `Name Restriction Facts` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`an undesirable name` MEANS `Name Restriction Facts` OF TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`a name identical to an existing name` MEANS `Name Restriction Facts` OF FALSE, TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`a name identical to a reserved name` MEANS `Name Restriction Facts` OF FALSE, FALSE, TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE
`a name of a kind the Minister directed not to accept` MEANS `Name Restriction Facts` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE,  FALSE
`an undesirable name with the Minister's consent` MEANS `Name Restriction Facts` OF TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE
`a name identical to an existing name, with the Minister's consent` MEANS `Name Restriction Facts` OF FALSE, TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, TRUE

#ASSERT NOT `section 17(1) bars the name` `an acceptable name` FALSE
#ASSERT `section 17(1) bars the name` `an undesirable name` FALSE
#ASSERT `section 17(1) bars the name` `a name identical to an existing name` FALSE
#ASSERT `section 17(1) bars the name` `a name identical to a reserved name` FALSE
#ASSERT `section 17(1) bars the name` `a name of a kind the Minister directed not to accept` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `section 17(1) bars the name` `an undesirable name with the Minister's consent` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `section 17(1) bars the name` `a name identical to an existing name, with the Minister's consent` FALSE
-- 17(3) lifts the bar for an identical name only
#ASSERT NOT `section 17(1) bars the name` `a name identical to an existing name` TRUE
#ASSERT `section 17(1) bars the name` `an undesirable name` TRUE
#ASSERT `section 17(1) bars the name` `a name identical to a reserved name` TRUE

-- 17(2): waiting periods
`a business name cancelled on 1 March 2025` MEANS `the business name of a person whose registration was cancelled under this Act or has ceased under section 22` (YMD 2025 3 1)
`a company wound up and dissolved on 1 March 2024` MEANS `the name of a company dissolved following its winding up under Part 8 of the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018` (YMD 2024 3 1)
`a company struck off on 1 March 2020` MEANS `the name of a company dissolved following its name being struck off under section 344 or 344A of the Companies Act 1967` (YMD 2020 3 1)
`a foreign company dissolved on 1 March 2024` MEANS `the name of a foreign company of whose dissolution notice has been given under section 377(2) of the Companies Act 1967` (YMD 2024 3 1)
`an LLP wound up on 1 March 2024` MEANS `the name of a limited liability partnership dissolved following its winding up` (YMD 2024 3 1)
`an LLP struck off on 1 March 2020` MEANS `the name of a limited liability partnership dissolved following its name being struck off under section 63 of the Limited Liability Partnerships Act 2005` (YMD 2020 3 1)
`a limited partnership cancelled on 1 March 2025` MEANS `the name of a limited partnership whose registration was cancelled under section 14(1) or 19(4) of the Limited Partnerships Act 2008` (YMD 2025 3 1)
`a limited partnership dissolved on 1 March 2025` MEANS `the name of a limited partnership dissolved under section 19(2) of the Limited Partnerships Act 2008` (YMD 2025 3 1)

#ASSERT `the waiting period in years after an earlier use of the name` `a business name cancelled on 1 March 2025` EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `the waiting period in years after an earlier use of the name` `a company wound up and dissolved on 1 March 2024` EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `the waiting period in years after an earlier use of the name` `a company struck off on 1 March 2020` EQUALS 6
#ASSERT `the waiting period in years after an earlier use of the name` `a foreign company dissolved on 1 March 2024` EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `the waiting period in years after an earlier use of the name` `an LLP wound up on 1 March 2024` EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `the waiting period in years after an earlier use of the name` `an LLP struck off on 1 March 2020` EQUALS 6
#ASSERT `the waiting period in years after an earlier use of the name` `a limited partnership cancelled on 1 March 2025` EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `the waiting period in years after an earlier use of the name` `a limited partnership dissolved on 1 March 2025` EQUALS 1

-- one year after cancellation: 28 February 2026 is a day short, 1 March 2026 is the anniversary
#ASSERT `section 17(2) bars the name` `a business name cancelled on 1 March 2025` (YMD 2026 2 28) FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `section 17(2) bars the name` `a business name cancelled on 1 March 2025` (YMD 2026 3 1) FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `section 17(2) bars the name` `a business name cancelled on 1 March 2025` (YMD 2026 2 28) TRUE
#ASSERT `section 17(2) bars the name` `a company wound up and dissolved on 1 March 2024` (YMD 2026 2 28) FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `section 17(2) bars the name` `a company wound up and dissolved on 1 March 2024` (YMD 2026 3 1) FALSE
#ASSERT `section 17(2) bars the name` `a company struck off on 1 March 2020` (YMD 2026 2 28) FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `section 17(2) bars the name` `a company struck off on 1 March 2020` (YMD 2026 3 1) FALSE
#ASSERT `section 17(2) bars the name` `an LLP struck off on 1 March 2020` (YMD 2026 2 28) FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `section 17(2) bars the name` `an LLP struck off on 1 March 2020` (YMD 2026 3 1) FALSE
#ASSERT `section 17(2) bars the name` `a limited partnership dissolved on 1 March 2025` (YMD 2026 2 28) FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `section 17(2) bars the name` `a limited partnership dissolved on 1 March 2025` (YMD 2026 3 1) FALSE

-- 17(3): the periods after which an identical name may be registered
`a foreign company that ceased business on 15 January 2026` MEANS `the name of a foreign company that lodged notice under section 377(1) of the Companies Act 1967 that it ceased to have a place of business or to carry on business in Singapore` (YMD 2026 1 15)
`a foreign company struck off on 1 March 2020` MEANS `the name of a foreign company struck off under section 377(8), (9) or (10) of the Companies Act 1967` (YMD 2020 3 1)
`a limited partnership that ceased business on 1 March 2025` MEANS `the name of a limited partnership that lodged notice under section 19(1) of the Limited Partnerships Act 2008 that it ceased to carry on business in Singapore` (YMD 2025 3 1)

#ASSERT NOT `section 17(3) permits registration of the name` `a foreign company that ceased business on 15 January 2026` (YMD 2026 4 14)
#ASSERT `section 17(3) permits registration of the name` `a foreign company that ceased business on 15 January 2026` (YMD 2026 4 15)
#ASSERT NOT `section 17(3) permits registration of the name` `a foreign company struck off on 1 March 2020` (YMD 2026 2 28)
#ASSERT `section 17(3) permits registration of the name` `a foreign company struck off on 1 March 2020` (YMD 2026 3 1)
#ASSERT NOT `section 17(3) permits registration of the name` `a limited partnership that ceased business on 1 March 2025` (YMD 2026 2 28)
#ASSERT `section 17(3) permits registration of the name` `a limited partnership that ceased business on 1 March 2025` (YMD 2026 3 1)

-- 17(4): grounds for a direction.  Direction Grounds Facts: barred under 17(1)(a),(b),(d); barred under
-- 17(2) until the period expires; permitted under 17(3) only after the period; resembles another
-- name; restrained by a Trade Marks Act injunction.
#ASSERT `the Registrar may direct the person to change the registered business name` (`Direction Grounds Facts` OF TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE)
#ASSERT `the Registrar may direct the person to change the registered business name` (`Direction Grounds Facts` OF FALSE, TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, FALSE)
#ASSERT `the Registrar may direct the person to change the registered business name` (`Direction Grounds Facts` OF FALSE, FALSE, TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE)
#ASSERT `the Registrar may direct the person to change the registered business name` (`Direction Grounds Facts` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE,  FALSE)
#ASSERT `the Registrar may direct the person to change the registered business name` (`Direction Grounds Facts` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `the Registrar may direct the person to change the registered business name` (`Direction Grounds Facts` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE)

-- Direction Facts: date of direction, longer period allowed, date the name changed, date registered or
-- change approved, date the application under s 17(6) was received, ground is likeness.
`a direction on 1 March 2026` MEANS `Direction Facts` OF YMD 2026 3 1, NOTHING, JUST (YMD 2026 4 12), YMD 2026 3 1, YMD 2026 3 1, FALSE
`a direction on 1 March 2026, complied with a day late` MEANS `Direction Facts` OF YMD 2026 3 1, NOTHING, JUST (YMD 2026 4 13), YMD 2026 3 1, YMD 2026 3 1, FALSE
`a direction on 1 March 2026, not complied with` MEANS `Direction Facts` OF YMD 2026 3 1, NOTHING, NOTHING, YMD 2026 3 1, YMD 2026 3 1, FALSE
`a direction on 1 March 2026 with a longer period to 1 May` MEANS `Direction Facts` OF YMD 2026 3 1, JUST (YMD 2026 5 1), JUST (YMD 2026 5 1), YMD 2026 3 1, YMD 2026 3 1, FALSE
`a direction on 1 March 2026 with an allowance shorter than 6 weeks` MEANS `Direction Facts` OF YMD 2026 3 1, JUST (YMD 2026 3 20), JUST (YMD 2026 4 12), YMD 2026 3 1, YMD 2026 3 1, FALSE

#ASSERT `the last day for complying with the Registrar's direction` `a direction on 1 March 2026` EQUALS YMD 2026 4 12
#ASSERT `the last day for complying with the Registrar's direction` `a direction on 1 March 2026 with a longer period to 1 May` EQUALS YMD 2026 5 1
#ASSERT `the last day for complying with the Registrar's direction` `a direction on 1 March 2026 with an allowance shorter than 6 weeks` EQUALS YMD 2026 4 12
#ASSERT `the person complied with the direction in time` `a direction on 1 March 2026`
#ASSERT NOT `the person complied with the direction in time` `a direction on 1 March 2026, complied with a day late`
#ASSERT NOT `the person complied with the direction in time` `a direction on 1 March 2026, not complied with`
#ASSERT `the person complied with the direction in time` `a direction on 1 March 2026 with a longer period to 1 May`
#ASSERT `the Registrar may cancel for failure to comply with the direction` `a direction on 1 March 2026, complied with a day late` (YMD 2026 4 13)
#ASSERT NOT `the Registrar may cancel for failure to comply with the direction` `a direction on 1 March 2026, complied with a day late` (YMD 2026 4 12)
#ASSERT `the Registrar may cancel for failure to comply with the direction` `a direction on 1 March 2026, not complied with` (YMD 2026 4 13)
#ASSERT NOT `the Registrar may cancel for failure to comply with the direction` `a direction on 1 March 2026` (YMD 2026 4 13)

#TRACE `the duty to change the registered business name as directed` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `The registrant` DOES `change the registered business name as the Registrar directed` AT 42

#TRACE `the duty to change the registered business name as directed` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 43)

-- 17(7): an application on the ground of likeness must be received within 12 months
`a likeness application received on the anniversary` MEANS `Direction Facts` OF YMD 2026 3 1, NOTHING, NOTHING, YMD 2026 3 1, YMD 2027 3 1, TRUE
`a likeness application received a day after the anniversary` MEANS `Direction Facts` OF YMD 2026 3 1, NOTHING, NOTHING, YMD 2026 3 1, YMD 2027 3 2, TRUE
`another application years later` MEANS `Direction Facts` OF YMD 2026 3 1, NOTHING, NOTHING, YMD 2026 3 1, YMD 2030 3 2, FALSE

#ASSERT `the Registrar may consider the application for a direction` `a likeness application received on the anniversary`
#ASSERT NOT `the Registrar may consider the application for a direction` `a likeness application received a day after the anniversary`
#ASSERT `the Registrar may consider the application for a direction` `another application years later`

§§ `18. Change of registered business name`

-- Name Change Facts: lodged, approved, new name must be refused under s 17, Minister consents.
#ASSERT `the Registrar is to issue a notice of change of registered business name` (`Name Change Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the Registrar is to issue a notice of change of registered business name` (`Name Change Facts` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE)
