§§ `23. Cancellation of registration`

-- Non-trading Facts: reasonable cause, written notice given, date of notice, date objections are due,
-- person answered that it is not carrying on business, date an objection was received.
`a notice of 1 March 2026 asking for objections by 31 March 2026` MEANS `Non-trading Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, YMD 2026 3 1, YMD 2026 3 31, FALSE, NOTHING
`a notice of 1 March 2026 asking for objections by 30 March 2026` MEANS `Non-trading Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, YMD 2026 3 1, YMD 2026 3 30, FALSE, NOTHING
`an objection on the 30th day` MEANS `Non-trading Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, YMD 2026 3 1, YMD 2026 3 31, FALSE, JUST (YMD 2026 3 31)
`an objection on the 31st day` MEANS `Non-trading Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, YMD 2026 3 1, YMD 2026 3 31, FALSE, JUST (YMD 2026 4 1)
`an answer that the person is not trading, despite an objection` MEANS `Non-trading Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, YMD 2026 3 1, YMD 2026 3 31, TRUE, JUST (YMD 2026 3 10)
`no reasonable cause` MEANS `Non-trading Facts` OF FALSE, TRUE, YMD 2026 3 1, YMD 2026 3 31, FALSE, NOTHING
`no written notice given` MEANS `Non-trading Facts` OF TRUE, FALSE, YMD 2026 3 1, YMD 2026 3 31, FALSE, NOTHING

#ASSERT `the Registrar may give notice proposing to cancel` `a notice of 1 March 2026 asking for objections by 31 March 2026`
#ASSERT NOT `the Registrar may give notice proposing to cancel` `no reasonable cause`
#ASSERT `the notice allows enough time for objection` `a notice of 1 March 2026 asking for objections by 31 March 2026`
#ASSERT NOT `the notice allows enough time for objection` `a notice of 1 March 2026 asking for objections by 30 March 2026`
#ASSERT `the Registrar may cancel the registration under section 23` `a notice of 1 March 2026 asking for objections by 31 March 2026`
#ASSERT NOT `the Registrar may cancel the registration under section 23` `a notice of 1 March 2026 asking for objections by 30 March 2026`
#ASSERT NOT `the Registrar may cancel the registration under section 23` `an objection on the 30th day`
#ASSERT `the Registrar may cancel the registration under section 23` `an objection on the 31st day`
#ASSERT `the Registrar may cancel the registration under section 23` `an answer that the person is not trading, despite an objection`
#ASSERT NOT `the Registrar may cancel the registration under section 23` `no reasonable cause`
#ASSERT NOT `the Registrar may cancel the registration under section 23` `no written notice given`
#ASSERT `any certificate or notice pertaining to the registration is taken to be cancelled` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `any certificate or notice pertaining to the registration is taken to be cancelled` FALSE

§§ `24. Restoration of registration`

-- Restoration Facts: how the registration ended, date it ended, date the application is lodged, Registrar
-- allows a longer time, a s 9 restriction applies, outstanding fees paid, late renewal penalty paid.
`cancelled under section 14 on 1 March 2026, application on the anniversary` MEANS `Restoration Facts` OF `cancelled under section 14`, YMD 2026 3 1, YMD 2027 3 1, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE
`cancelled under section 14 on 1 March 2026, application a day late` MEANS `Restoration Facts` OF `cancelled under section 14`, YMD 2026 3 1, YMD 2027 3 2, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE
`cancelled under section 14, a day late but the Registrar allows longer` MEANS `Restoration Facts` OF `cancelled under section 14`, YMD 2026 3 1, YMD 2027 3 2, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE
`cancelled under section 12(2)` MEANS `Restoration Facts` OF `cancelled under section 12(2)`, YMD 2026 3 1, YMD 2026 6 1, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE
`cancelled under section 23` MEANS `Restoration Facts` OF `cancelled under section 23`, YMD 2026 3 1, YMD 2026 6 1, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE
`ceased under section 22` MEANS `Restoration Facts` OF `ceased under section 22`, YMD 2026 3 1, YMD 2026 6 1, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE
`ended in another way` MEANS `Restoration Facts` OF `ended in another way`, YMD 2026 3 1, YMD 2026 6 1, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE
`a restoration barred by section 9` MEANS `Restoration Facts` OF `cancelled under section 14`, YMD 2026 3 1, YMD 2026 6 1, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE
`a restoration with fees unpaid` MEANS `Restoration Facts` OF `cancelled under section 14`, YMD 2026 3 1, YMD 2026 6 1, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE
`a restoration with the late penalty unpaid` MEANS `Restoration Facts` OF `cancelled under section 14`, YMD 2026 3 1, YMD 2026 6 1, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE

#ASSERT `the person may apply to restore the registration` `cancelled under section 12(2)`
#ASSERT `the person may apply to restore the registration` `cancelled under section 14 on 1 March 2026, application on the anniversary`
#ASSERT `the person may apply to restore the registration` `cancelled under section 23`
#ASSERT `the person may apply to restore the registration` `ceased under section 22`
#ASSERT NOT `the person may apply to restore the registration` `ended in another way`
#ASSERT `the application to restore is made in time` `cancelled under section 14 on 1 March 2026, application on the anniversary`
#ASSERT NOT `the application to restore is made in time` `cancelled under section 14 on 1 March 2026, application a day late`
#ASSERT `the application to restore is made in time` `cancelled under section 14, a day late but the Registrar allows longer`
#ASSERT `the Registrar may grant the application to restore` `cancelled under section 14 on 1 March 2026, application on the anniversary`
#ASSERT NOT `the Registrar may grant the application to restore` `cancelled under section 14 on 1 March 2026, application a day late`
#ASSERT `the Registrar may grant the application to restore` `cancelled under section 14, a day late but the Registrar allows longer`
#ASSERT NOT `the Registrar may grant the application to restore` `ended in another way`
#ASSERT NOT `the Registrar may grant the application to restore` `a restoration barred by section 9`
#ASSERT NOT `the Registrar may grant the application to restore` `a restoration with fees unpaid`
#ASSERT NOT `the Registrar may grant the application to restore` `a restoration with the late penalty unpaid`
#ASSERT `the registration is treated as if it had not been cancelled or had not ceased` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the registration is treated as if it had not been cancelled or had not ceased` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `restoration prevents prosecution for an offence under section 35(1)(a)`
